    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d530">

                <pb facs="1033" n="1021" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg1021"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by General Hsu Yung-chang to General
                        Marshall</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-10">10 June 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear General Marshall</hi>: This is to notify you
                    that in my conversation with you yesterday afternoon (9th June) you contemplated
                    to amend slightly, items (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) and (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">c</hi>) in the proposed “Agreement to <pb facs="1034"
                        n="1022" xml:id="pg1022"/> Insure the More Expeditious Functioning of
                    Executive Headquarters”.<anchor n="48" xml:id="d530-f1"/></p>
                <p>The Generalissimo’s opinion is that except the words “and decisions covering the
                    local situation” in item (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) may be altered, item
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) should remain the same as you originally
                    proposed without any change.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hsu Yung Chang</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">seal</hi>)</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
